                    insight_earned:         `Authority earned: you turned a title into legitimacy the squad granted you — answering on the merits, earning the veteran back, deciding in the open, and naming the rules of the game. This is the promotion that doesn't become the 5th failure.`,
                    insight_rank:           `You pulled rank in an expert culture, and the room remembers. Asserted authority is forfeited authority here — the skeptic has his proof, and trust never recovered. Win on reasoning, not the badge.`,
                    insight_abdicate:       `You deferred to seem collaborative and left a leadership vacuum. Followers grant authority to a leader who will decide — abdication forfeits authority as surely as domination does. The squad needed your call, not your consensus.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of earning the room. Re-examine where you over-asserted or over-questioned, and which member's consent you never won — most likely the passed-over veteran.`,
                    insight_lowfollower:    `Follower engagement stayed low: the skeptic and the veteran never chose to follow. Authority is conferred by followers — without their consent the title is just a chair.`,
                    insight_lowself:        `Self-awareness stayed low — you performed certainty instead of reflecting honestly. In a Learning-Teams culture, admitting what you don't yet know builds more durable authority than projecting that you know everything.`,
                    insight_nocontract:     `You never set an explicit leadership contract. The squad still doesn't know when you'll open the floor and when you'll decide — that ambiguity is exactly what drove your predecessors' velocity collapse.`,
                    insight_credburn:       `Your credibility capital ran low: too many moves reached for the badge in a culture that reads it instantly. In an expertise-based team, credibility is fragile and doesn't refill on demand.`,
                    insight_lasts:          `This is authority that lasts: trust, follower engagement and self-awareness moving together, with an explicit contract behind them. Six months from now the squad still grants you the room — and Helios kept its velocity.`,

                    hint_rank:              `You reached for the badge — and in this culture that's forfeited authority. Spend the remaining rounds rebuilding credibility through open reasoning and earning consent, not asserting it.`,
                    hint_abdicate:          `You're hiding behind consensus. Followers grant authority to a leader who decides. Before Friday, close a question and own the call — abdication is as fatal as domination here.`,
                    hint_follower:          `Follower engagement is dangerously low — the squad hasn't chosen to follow you. Focus on what the veteran and the skeptic each need to grant their consent; authority is conferred, not demanded.`,
                    hint_self:              `Self-awareness is weak — you're performing more than reflecting. Naming what you don't yet know is the Learning-Teams move that earns durable authority in this culture.`,
                    hint_behind:            `Trust is well behind with the Friday freeze closing in. Concentrate on the highest-leverage relationships — the skeptic's buy-in and the veteran's consent — not on asserting control.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — trust, follower engagement and self-awareness all healthy. Now lock it in with an explicit leadership contract so the authority survives past this week.`,

